public import WeilConjectures.FromJoel.CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.Retract

/-!
# Idempotent completeness of `D_comp(J, 𝒪_E)`

For an ideal `I = (ϖ)` generated by a nonzerodivisor, the derived complete objects of `D(J, R)`
are the right orthogonal of the objects on which `ϖ` acts invertibly
(`DerivedCategory.derivedComplete_iff_rightOrthogonal`), hence are stable under retracts. As
`D(J, R)` has coproducts, it is idempotent complete (Bökstedt–Neeman,
`CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.isIdempotentComplete_of_hasCoproducts`), and so is the full
subcategory `D_comp(J, 𝒪_E)` of derived complete objects.

## Main statements

- `DerivedCategory.isStableUnderRetracts_derivedComplete`
- `DerivedCategoryDerivedCompleteIntegral.isIdempotentComplete`
-/

@[expose] public section

universe w u

open CategoryTheory Limits

namespace DerivedCategory

variable {C : Type (u + 1)} [Category.{u} C] [EssentiallySmall.{u + 1} C]
  (J : GrothendieckTopology C) {R : Type (u + 1)} [CommRing R]

end DerivedCategory

section RingOfIntegers

variable {C : Type (u + 1)} [Category.{u} C] [EssentiallySmall.{u + 1} C]
  (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (l : ℕ) [Fact l.Prime] (E : Type w) [Field E]
  [Algebra E (PadicAlgCl l)] [Algebra ℚ_[l] E] [IsScalarTower ℚ_[l] E (PadicAlgCl l)]
  [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[l] E] [Small.{u + 1} E]

end RingOfIntegers
